                                "sense_id": "e8f578ab-7ed0-3790-89ef-c93ef49b2a2e",
                                "text": "If wit enhances meaning, this systematic reductiveness is antiwit, ultimately reduced to an infantile practical joke that backfires."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8dac100-eaba-48db-816d-09c1765b174f",
                                "sense_id": "e8f578ab-7ed0-3790-89ef-c93ef49b2a2e",
                                "text": "[…] that was rendered as a kind of brilliant, nonsensical antiwit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ca2b5eb-67ab-4792-8de8-1a31bc56961e",
                                "sense_id": "e8f578ab-7ed0-3790-89ef-c93ef49b2a2e",
                                "text": "\"He leaves Bowie laughing partly at the soporific antiwit,\" wrote Crowe, \"but mostly over a successful effort at producing the unproduceable. Less than a minute later, Iggy Pop is the farthest thing from his mind. Bowie's blanched bony face has already fallen into furrows. 'I am very, very bored,' he says.\""
                            }
